# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values. .env.local is
# gitignored by the Vite starter and should never be committed.
#
# Every variable in this file is a VITE_ variable, which means Vite compiles
# it directly into the JavaScript bundle every visitor downloads. That is fine
# here because Web3Forms access keys are designed to be public — the key only
# identifies which inbox a submission goes to, it grants no other access.
#
# Do not add any other kind of key to this file, or to any VITE_ variable
# anywhere in this project. A database URL, a Stripe secret key, an API key
# that grants write access, an OAuth client secret — none of those can live in
# src/. They belong server-side, in a Vercel serverless function under api/,
# reading a non-VITE_ environment variable set in the Vercel dashboard rather
# than committed anywhere. See api/README.md and docs/shop-architecture.md.

# Contact form submission target. Get one at https://web3forms.com — free,
# no account required beyond an email to receive submissions at.
# Without this set, the contact form falls back to a mailto: link instead of
# breaking.
VITE_WEB3FORMS_KEY=
